   "text": "I read the molecule as a maleimide\u2013PEG3\u2013Gly-Gly-Phe-Gly linker joined through an amide to a fluoro-amino camptothecin core, an exatecan-type payload.\n\n**Linker, left to right**\n1. A maleimide ring (`O=C1C=CC(=O)N1`) is attached through its nitrogen to the chain.\n2. The chain is CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O), so three ether oxygens.\n3. The peptide follows as NH\u2013Gly\u2013Gly\u2013Phe\u2013Gly, with a benzyl side chain on the Phe.\n4. The Phe \u03b1-carbon is drawn with a hashed bond to its CH2. I wrote this centre as `[C@@H]`.\n5. The last glycine carbonyl is bonded through NH to the aromatic ring of the core.\n\n**Camptothecin-type core**\n1. The benzo ring carries the NH on one carbon and F on the adjacent carbon.\n2. The benzo ring is fused to a pyridine (the ring N is labelled in the drawing).\n3. The pyridine is fused to a pyrroline CH2\u2013N ring, then to a pyridone (C=O on the ring N).\n4. The pyridone is fused to a lactone ring, OCH2 and C(=O)O.\n5. The lactone ring closes at a quaternary carbon bearing OH (bold wedge) and ethyl.\n\n**Stereochemistry at the quaternary carbon**\nI worked out the chirality from the wedge geometry. The result is `[C@]4(O)CC` when written after the lactone carbonyl, which matches the natural (S) camptothecin configuration.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)NCC(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)NCC(=O)Nc1cc2cc3c(nc2cc1F)-c1cc2c(c(=O)n1C3)COC(=O)[C@]2(O)CC"
